{
  "info": {
    "name": "wm-1015-bulk-owner",
    "description": "Réassignation en masse du champ `owner` des APIs d'une webMethods API Gateway 10.15.\n\nMÉCANISME (établi sur une 10.15 réelle le 2026-07-29) :\n  POST /rest/apigateway/assets/owner\n  { assetIds: [<id d'API>, ...], assetType: 'API', newOwner: '<valeur>', ownerType: 'user' }\n\nCE QUI NE MARCHE PAS, et pourquoi cette collection ne l'utilise pas :\n  PUT /rest/apigateway/apis/{id} avec le champ `owner` muté renvoie 200 et\n  N'A AUCUN EFFET. Le même PUT modifie bien `apiDescription` — `owner` est\n  géré par le serveur et silencieusement ignoré sur cet endpoint. Vérifié\n  aussi avec un owner correspondant à un utilisateur existant.\n\nTrois modes, pilotés par `runMode` :\n  - `probe`  : lit UNE API (`probeApiId`) et vérifie que `owner` est lisible. N'écrit rien.\n  - `dryRun` : liste, filtre, et rapporte `owner actuel -> owner cible`. N'écrit rien.\n  - `apply`  : écrit, PUIS RELIT chaque API pour vérifier que le changement a bien pris.\n\nÀ lancer avec le Collection Runner ou Newman UNIQUEMENT : la boucle repose sur\n`postman.setNextRequest`, sans effet en envoi manuel requête par requête.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "runMode",
      "value": "probe",
      "description": "probe | dryRun | apply"
    },
    {
      "key": "newOwner",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Nouvelle valeur du champ owner. Obligatoire en mode apply."
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerType",
      "value": "user",
      "description": "user | group — second membre du couple attendu par /assets/owner."
    },
    {
      "key": "filterNameContains",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Contains insensible à la casse sur apiName. Appliqué sur la LISTE. Vide = pas de contrainte."
    },
    {
      "key": "filterCurrentOwner",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Contains insensible à la casse sur l'owner courant. Appliqué sur le DÉTAIL de chaque API,\ncar l'endpoint de liste ne renvoie pas `owner`. Vide = pas de contrainte."
    },
    {
      "key": "probeApiId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "id d'une API quelconque, utilisée par la requête 00 en mode probe."
    },
    {
      "key": "maxApis",
      "value": "50",
      "description": "Garde-fou de volume, appliqué au filtrage par NOM (donc avant le filtre sur owner).\nIl majore la sélection réelle : c'est volontairement conservateur."
    },
    {
      "key": "scanQueue",
      "value": "[]"
    },
    {
      "key": "verifyQueue",
      "value": "[]"
    },
    {
      "key": "selected",
      "value": "[]"
    },
    {
      "key": "report",
      "value": "[]"
    },
    {
      "key": "currentApiId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerChangePayload",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 — Reconnaissance",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Porte de reconnaissance. N'écrit rien.",
              "// Vérifie que `owner` est lisible là où la suite de la collection le cherche.",
              "",
              "const mode = String(pm.variables.get('runMode') || '').trim();",
              "const probeApiId = String(pm.variables.get('probeApiId') || '').trim();",
              "",
              "pm.test('00 — runMode est valide', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(['probe', 'dryRun', 'apply']).to.include(mode);",
              "});",
              "",
              "// La reconnaissance n'a de sens qu'en mode probe : hors de ce mode on enchaîne",
              "// directement, sans exiger de probeApiId ni asserter sur cette réponse.",
              "if (mode !== 'probe') {",
              "    postman.setNextRequest('01 — Lister et filtrer par nom');",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('00 — probeApiId est renseigné', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(probeApiId, 'le mode probe exige un probeApiId').to.not.eql('');",
              "});",
              "if (probeApiId === '') { postman.setNextRequest(null); return; }",
              "",
              "pm.test('00 — la Gateway répond 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "let body = null;",
              "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
              "",
              "// Si la réponse est du HTML, c'est que l'en-tête Accept n'a pas été pris en compte :",
              "// l'Integration Server rend en HTML par défaut. Toutes les requêtes d'ici portent Accept.",
              "pm.test('00 — la réponse est bien du JSON (Accept: application/json honoré)', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body, 'réponse non-JSON — probable rendu HTML par défaut de l\\'IS').to.not.be.null;",
              "});",
              "",
              "let api = null;",
              "let shape = 'inconnue';",
              "if (body && body.apiResponse && body.apiResponse.api) { api = body.apiResponse.api; shape = 'apiResponse.api'; }",
              "else if (body && body.api) { api = body.api; shape = 'api'; }",
              "else if (body && body.apiName) { api = body; shape = 'racine'; }",
              "",
              "pm.test('00 — objet API localisé dans la réponse', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(api, 'objet API introuvable dans la réponse').to.be.an('object');",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (api) {",
              "    console.log('--- RECONNAISSANCE ------------------------------------------');",
              "    console.log('Enveloppe détectée        : ' + shape);",
              "    console.log('Clés de premier niveau    : ' + Object.keys(api).sort().join(', '));",
              "    console.log('owner (valeur brute)      : ' + JSON.stringify(api.owner));",
              "    console.log('owner (type)              : ' + typeof api.owner);",
              "    console.log('-------------------------------------------------------------');",
              "",
              "    pm.test(\"00 — le champ 'owner' est lisible sur le détail de l'API\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(api).to.have.property('owner');",
              "        pm.expect(api.owner).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "}",
              "",
              "if (mode === 'probe') {",
              "    console.log('Mode probe : arrêt après reconnaissance. Aucune écriture.');",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/apis/{{probeApiId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "apis",
            "{{probeApiId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lit une API au hasard pour vérifier que `owner` est lisible. Ne modifie rien."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "01 — Lister et filtrer par nom",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Premier étage du filtre : le NOM, seul critère disponible sur la liste.",
              "// L'endpoint de liste ne renvoie qu'une projection résumée",
              "// (apiName, apiVersion, id, isActive, type, ...) — PAS `owner`.",
              "// Le filtre sur owner est donc appliqué en 02, sur le détail de chaque API.",
              "",
              "const mode       = String(pm.variables.get('runMode') || '').trim();",
              "const newOwner   = String(pm.variables.get('newOwner') || '').trim();",
              "const nameNeedle = String(pm.variables.get('filterNameContains') || '').trim().toLowerCase();",
              "const ownNeedle  = String(pm.variables.get('filterCurrentOwner') || '').trim().toLowerCase();",
              "const maxApis    = parseInt(pm.variables.get('maxApis') || '50', 10);",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('report', '[]');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('selected', '[]');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('scanQueue', '[]');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('verifyQueue', '[]');",
              "",
              "pm.test('01 — la liste des APIs répond 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (mode === 'apply' && newOwner === '') {",
              "    pm.test('01 — apply exige un newOwner non vide', function () {",
              "        pm.expect.fail(\"runMode=apply mais newOwner est vide. Rien n'a été écrit.\");",
              "    });",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "let body = null;",
              "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
              "",
              "function extractApis(b) {",
              "    if (!b) { return []; }",
              "    let raw = b.apiResponse || b.apis || b;",
              "    if (!Array.isArray(raw)) { raw = raw.apiResponse || raw.apis || []; }",
              "    if (!Array.isArray(raw)) { return []; }",
              "    return raw",
              "        .map(function (e) { return (e && e.api) ? e.api : e; })",
              "        .filter(function (a) { return a && (a.id || a.apiId); });",
              "}",
              "",
              "const apis = extractApis(body);",
              "",
              "pm.test('01 — au moins une API lue depuis la Gateway', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(apis.length, 'aucune API extraite — la forme de la réponse a changé').to.be.above(0);",
              "});",
              "",
              "const scanQueue = apis",
              "    .filter(function (a) {",
              "        const n = String(a.apiName || '').toLowerCase();",
              "        return (nameNeedle === '') || (n.indexOf(nameNeedle) !== -1);",
              "    })",
              "    .map(function (a) {",
              "        return {",
              "            apiId:      a.id || a.apiId,",
              "            apiName:    a.apiName || '(sans nom)',",
              "            apiVersion: a.apiVersion || ''",
              "        };",
              "    });",
              "",
              "console.log('--- SÉLECTION (étage 1 : nom) -------------------------------');",
              "console.log('Mode                      : ' + mode);",
              "console.log('APIs lues                 : ' + apis.length);",
              "console.log('Filtre nom (contains)     : ' + (nameNeedle || '(aucun)'));",
              "console.log('Retenues sur le nom       : ' + scanQueue.length);",
              "console.log('Filtre owner (contains)   : ' + (ownNeedle || '(aucun)') + '  [appliqué en 02]');",
              "console.log('-------------------------------------------------------------');",
              "",
              "if (scanQueue.length > maxApis) {",
              "    pm.test('01 — garde-fou de volume', function () {",
              "        pm.expect.fail(",
              "            scanQueue.length + ' APIs retenues sur le nom pour un maxApis de ' + maxApis + '. ' +",
              "            \"Rien n'a été écrit. Resserrer filterNameContains, ou relever maxApis en conscience.\"",
              "        );",
              "    });",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('scanQueue', JSON.stringify(scanQueue));",
              "",
              "if (scanQueue.length === 0) {",
              "    console.log('Aucune API ne correspond au filtre sur le nom.');",
              "    postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport');",
              "} else {",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(\"02 — Lire l'owner courant\");",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/apis",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "apis"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liste toutes les APIs et applique le filtre Contains sur le nom."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — Lire l'owner courant",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const q = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('scanQueue') || '[]');",
              "if (q.length === 0) {",
              "    postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport');",
              "} else {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentApiId', q[0].apiId);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Second étage du filtre : l'OWNER, lisible seulement sur le détail.",
              "// Boucle EN LECTURE SEULE. Aucune écriture n'a lieu ici, quel que soit le mode.",
              "",
              "const mode      = String(pm.variables.get('runMode') || '').trim();",
              "const newOwner  = String(pm.variables.get('newOwner') || '').trim();",
              "const ownNeedle = String(pm.variables.get('filterCurrentOwner') || '').trim().toLowerCase();",
              "const scanQueue = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('scanQueue') || '[]');",
              "const selected  = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('selected') || '[]');",
              "const report    = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('report') || '[]');",
              "const item      = scanQueue[0];",
              "",
              "function advance() {",
              "    scanQueue.shift();",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scanQueue', JSON.stringify(scanQueue));",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('selected', JSON.stringify(selected));",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('report', JSON.stringify(report));",
              "    if (scanQueue.length > 0) {",
              "        postman.setNextRequest(\"02 — Lire l'owner courant\");",
              "    } else if (mode === 'apply' && selected.length > 0) {",
              "        postman.setNextRequest('03 — Changer les owners');",
              "    } else {",
              "        postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport');",
              "    }",
              "}",
              "",
              "if (!item) { postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport'); return; }",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
              "    pm.test('02 — jeton refusé (401)', function () {",
              "        pm.expect.fail('Jeton expiré ou invalide. Arrêt au balayage de ' + item.apiName + '. Aucune écriture.');",
              "    });",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('02 — lecture de ' + item.apiName + ' ' + item.apiVersion, function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code !== 200) {",
              "    report.push({ api: item.apiName, version: item.apiVersion, statut: 'KO_LECTURE',",
              "                  de: '?', vers: newOwner, detail: 'HTTP ' + pm.response.code });",
              "    advance();",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "let api = null;",
              "try {",
              "    const b = pm.response.json();",
              "    api = (b.apiResponse && b.apiResponse.api) ? b.apiResponse.api : (b.api || b);",
              "} catch (e) { api = null; }",
              "",
              "const currentOwner = api ? String(api.owner || '') : '';",
              "",
              "// Filtre owner : Contains insensible à la casse.",
              "if (ownNeedle !== '' && currentOwner.toLowerCase().indexOf(ownNeedle) === -1) {",
              "    report.push({ api: item.apiName, version: item.apiVersion, statut: 'HORS_FILTRE',",
              "                  de: currentOwner, vers: newOwner, detail: \"owner courant hors filtre\" });",
              "    advance();",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "// Déjà à la bonne valeur : on ne la réécrit pas.",
              "if (currentOwner === newOwner && newOwner !== '') {",
              "    report.push({ api: item.apiName, version: item.apiVersion, statut: 'DEJA_A_JOUR',",
              "                  de: currentOwner, vers: newOwner, detail: '' });",
              "    advance();",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "selected.push({ apiId: item.apiId, apiName: item.apiName,",
              "                apiVersion: item.apiVersion, currentOwner: currentOwner });",
              "",
              "if (mode === 'dryRun') {",
              "    report.push({ api: item.apiName, version: item.apiVersion, statut: 'DRY_RUN',",
              "                  de: currentOwner, vers: newOwner, detail: 'aucune écriture' });",
              "}",
              "",
              "advance();"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/apis/{{currentApiId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "apis",
            "{{currentApiId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lit le détail pour obtenir `owner`, absent de l'endpoint de liste. Lecture seule."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — Changer les owners",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// UNE SEULE requête pour tout le lot : /assets/owner accepte une LISTE d'assetIds.",
              "",
              "const selected  = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('selected') || '[]');",
              "const newOwner  = String(pm.variables.get('newOwner') || '').trim();",
              "const ownerType = String(pm.variables.get('ownerType') || 'user').trim();",
              "",
              "const payload = {",
              "    assetIds:  selected.map(function (s) { return s.apiId; }),",
              "    assetType: 'API',",
              "    newOwner:  newOwner,",
              "    ownerType: ownerType",
              "};",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('ownerChangePayload', JSON.stringify(payload));",
              "console.log('POST /assets/owner sur ' + payload.assetIds.length + ' API(s) -> ' + newOwner);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const selected = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('selected') || '[]');",
              "const report   = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('report') || '[]');",
              "const newOwner = String(pm.variables.get('newOwner') || '').trim();",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
              "    pm.test('03 — jeton refusé (401)', function () {",
              "        pm.expect.fail('Jeton expiré ou invalide. Aucun changement de propriétaire appliqué.');",
              "    });",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('03 — le changement de propriétaire est accepté', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "console.log('Réponse : ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 300));",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code !== 200) {",
              "    selected.forEach(function (s) {",
              "        report.push({ api: s.apiName, version: s.apiVersion, statut: 'KO_ECRITURE',",
              "                      de: s.currentOwner, vers: newOwner,",
              "                      detail: 'HTTP ' + pm.response.code + ' : ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 150) });",
              "    });",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('report', JSON.stringify(report));",
              "    postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport');",
              "    return;",
              "}",
              "",
              "// Un 200 de cette Gateway ne prouve RIEN : sur PUT /apis/{id}, le champ owner",
              "// est ignoré silencieusement avec un 200. On relit donc chaque API avant de conclure.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('verifyQueue', JSON.stringify(selected));",
              "postman.setNextRequest('04 — Vérifier');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{{ownerChangePayload}}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/assets/owner",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "assets",
            "owner"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Change le propriétaire de TOUTES les APIs sélectionnées en un seul appel."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "04 — Vérifier",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const q = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('verifyQueue') || '[]');",
              "if (q.length === 0) {",
              "    postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport');",
              "} else {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('currentApiId', q[0].apiId);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Contre-épreuve. Relit chaque API touchée et compare l'owner à la valeur voulue.",
              "// Sans cette étape, un 200 sans effet passerait pour un succès.",
              "",
              "const newOwner    = String(pm.variables.get('newOwner') || '').trim();",
              "const verifyQueue = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('verifyQueue') || '[]');",
              "const report      = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('report') || '[]');",
              "const item        = verifyQueue[0];",
              "",
              "if (!item) { postman.setNextRequest('05 — Rapport'); return; }",
              "",
              "let observed = null;",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    try {",
              "        const b = pm.response.json();",
              "        const api = (b.apiResponse && b.apiResponse.api) ? b.apiResponse.api : (b.api || b);",
              "        observed = String(api.owner || '');",
              "    } catch (e) { observed = null; }",
              "}",
              "",
              "const applique = (observed === newOwner);",
              "",
              "pm.test('04 — ' + item.apiName + ' : owner effectivement à \"' + newOwner + '\"', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(observed, 'owner relu sur la Gateway').to.eql(newOwner);",
              "});",
              "",
              "report.push({",
              "    api: item.apiName, version: item.apiVersion,",
              "    statut: applique ? 'OK' : 'KO_NON_APPLIQUE',",
              "    de: item.currentOwner, vers: newOwner,",
              "    detail: applique ? '' : ('relu : ' + JSON.stringify(observed) + \" — la Gateway a répondu 200 sans appliquer\")",
              "});",
              "",
              "verifyQueue.shift();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('verifyQueue', JSON.stringify(verifyQueue));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('report', JSON.stringify(report));",
              "postman.setNextRequest(verifyQueue.length > 0 ? '04 — Vérifier' : '05 — Rapport');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/apis/{{currentApiId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "apis",
            "{{currentApiId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Relit l'API pour prouver que le changement a réellement pris."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "05 — Rapport",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const mode   = String(pm.variables.get('runMode') || '').trim();",
              "const report = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('report') || '[]');",
              "",
              "function count(s) { return report.filter(function (r) { return r.statut === s; }).length; }",
              "const ko = report.filter(function (r) { return r.statut.indexOf('KO') === 0; });",
              "",
              "console.log('');",
              "console.log('=== RAPPORT (' + mode + ') =================================');",
              "if (report.length === 0) {",
              "    console.log('Aucune API traitée.');",
              "} else {",
              "    report.forEach(function (r) {",
              "        console.log('[' + r.statut + '] ' + r.api + ' ' + r.version +",
              "                    ' | ' + (r.de || '(vide)') + ' -> ' + (r.vers || '(vide)') +",
              "                    (r.detail ? ' | ' + r.detail : ''));",
              "    });",
              "}",
              "console.log('-------------------------------------------------------------');",
              "console.log('OK ' + count('OK') +",
              "            '  |  DRY_RUN ' + count('DRY_RUN') +",
              "            '  |  DEJA_A_JOUR ' + count('DEJA_A_JOUR') +",
              "            '  |  HORS_FILTRE ' + count('HORS_FILTRE') +",
              "            '  |  KO ' + ko.length);",
              "if (mode === 'dryRun') {",
              "    console.log('');",
              "    console.log('RELIRE CETTE LISTE LIGNE À LIGNE avant de passer en apply.');",
              "    console.log(\"Le filtre Contains sur un champ texte libre sur-matche par nature :\");",
              "    console.log(\"c'est ici, et seulement ici, que ça se voit.\");",
              "}",
              "console.log('=============================================================');",
              "",
              "pm.test('05 — aucun échec dans le lot', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(ko.length, ko.map(function (r) { return r.api; }).join(', ')).to.eql(0);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gwUrl}}/rest/apigateway/health",
          "host": [
            "{{gwUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rest",
            "apigateway",
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Support du rapport final. Ne modifie rien."
      }
    }
  ]
}
